---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CareerPathStories from "../../components/CareerPathStories.astro";
import CareersCrosslink from "../../components/CareersCrosslink.astro";
import { BRAND } from "../../constants/brand";
import { HIRING_IMAGES } from "../../constants/images";
import { hrefPath } from "../../lib/assets";
import { PAGE_SEO } from "../../lib/seo";

const IMG = HIRING_IMAGES;
---
<BaseLayout
  title={PAGE_SEO.careerPath.title}
  description={PAGE_SEO.careerPath.description}
  ogImage={PAGE_SEO.careerPath.ogImage}
  ogImageAlt="Allied CDL driver in front of a truck"
  bodyClass="career-path-page"
>
  <section class="page-band page-band--career">
    <div class="page-band__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Career progression</p>
      <h1>Your path forward at Bailey&apos;s</h1>
      <p class="sub">
        Moving is hard work — but if you do it well, there&apos;s real opportunity here. Not just a
        job, but a career that rewards performance and grows as you grow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="page-wrap career-path">
    <section class="career-path__intro content-card">
      <p class="section-label">The roadmap</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">From crew member to team leader to CDL driver</h2>
      <p class="lead career-path__lead">
        This page explains exactly how to advance — and what it takes at every step. The path is
        clear, the standards are fair, and the opportunity is real. You have to earn it.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        <strong>Who this is for:</strong> If you&apos;re starting as a mover and wondering
        what&apos;s ahead, this is your roadmap.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="career-step" id="step-requirements">
      <div class="career-step__content">
        <p class="career-step__label">Step 1</p>
        <h2 class="career-step__title">Meet the requirements</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Before you can lead a crew or drive a truck, you need to clear three basic requirements.
        </p>

        <h3 class="career-step__subtitle">Clean driving record</h3>
        <p class="career-step__text">
          We&apos;ll pull your Motor Vehicle Record (MVR). Here&apos;s what we&apos;re looking for:
        </p>
        <ul class="career-list">
          <li>No points on your license in the last 3–5 years</li>
          <li>No accidents in the last 3–5 years</li>
          <li>No traffic tickets or moving violations in the last 2 years</li>
          <li>No major violations (DUI, hit-and-run, etc.) in the last 10+ years</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="career-step__subtitle">Drug test</h3>
        <p class="career-step__text">
          You&apos;ll need to pass a standard DOT drug screening. We test for marijuana, cocaine,
          opiates, amphetamines and methamphetamines, and phencyclidine (PCP).
          <a
            href="https://www.fmcsa.dot.gov/regulations/drug-alcohol-testing/which-substances-are-tested"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="career-inline-link"
          >Learn more about DOT drug testing →</a>
        </p>

        <h3 class="career-step__subtitle">Background check</h3>
        <p class="career-step__text">
          We run a background screening that meets state, federal, and insurance requirements.
          We&apos;re looking for serious disqualifying offenses — violent felonies, theft, or fraud
          that would make it inappropriate to work inside customers&apos; homes or operate a company
          vehicle. If you have questions about your background, talk to your manager before starting
          the process.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="career-step__media">
        <img src={IMG.heroMover} alt="Bailey's mover with furniture in front of an Allied truck" width="600" height="400" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="career-step career-step--reverse" id="step-skills">
      <div class="career-step__content">
        <p class="career-step__label">Step 2</p>
        <h2 class="career-step__title">Prove your skills as a mover</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          You can&apos;t lead a crew if you can&apos;t do the job yourself. Before a leadership role,
          you need to show you&apos;re skilled enough to train others.
        </p>
        <p class="career-step__text">That means being genuinely good at:</p>
        <ul class="career-list">
          <li>Loading and unloading trucks</li>
          <li>Packing and protecting items</li>
          <li>Working efficiently as part of a team</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="career-step__text">
          For most people, reaching this level takes <strong>2–4 years</strong> of consistent work.
          Push hard, stay coachable, and it can happen faster. Operations leadership will confirm
          your readiness through a skills evaluation or your track record on the job.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="career-callout">
          <strong>Not there yet?</strong> That&apos;s fine. Keep building experience as a mover
          first. A stronger foundation makes you a better leader.
        </blockquote>
      </div>
      <figure class="career-step__media">
        <img src={IMG.packers} alt="Two crew members lifting a walkboard on a move" width="600" height="400" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="career-step" id="step-lead">
      <div class="career-step__content">
        <p class="career-step__label">Step 3</p>
        <h2 class="career-step__title">Lead your first move</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Once you&apos;re ready, operations will train you to run a moving job from start to finish.
          Your job is to consistently deliver <strong>five key outcomes</strong> on every move:
        </p>
        <ol class="career-outcomes">
          <li><strong>Start and finish on time.</strong> Every job. Every time.</li>
          <li><strong>Hit productivity targets.</strong> Every crew member meets minimum standards for loading, unloading, and/or packing.</li>
          <li><strong>Lead with confidence.</strong> Your team and customer are comfortable with your communication and decisions.</li>
          <li><strong>Complete your paperwork.</strong> Return with organized, complete, signed documents — nothing missing.</li>
          <li><strong>Earn a 5-star move.</strong> Work good enough for a 5-star review, whether the customer leaves one or not.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <figure class="career-step__media">
        <img src={IMG.family} alt="Young family smiling after a successful move" width="600" height="427" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="career-step career-step--reverse" id="step-drive">
      <div class="career-step__content">
        <p class="career-step__label">Step 4</p>
        <h2 class="career-step__title">Get behind the wheel</h2>
        <p class="lead">
          Driving the truck is a big step. It comes with dedicated training and a formal road test.
        </p>

        <h3 class="career-step__subtitle">Training</h3>
        <p class="career-step__text">
          You&apos;ll complete the <strong>Smith System Driver Training</strong> — a nationally
          recognized, safety-focused program used across the trucking and moving industry.
        </p>

        <h3 class="career-step__subtitle">Road test</h3>
        <p class="career-step__text">
          You&apos;ll take a practical road test with operations leadership and/or the safety
          director before you&apos;re cleared to drive on jobs.
        </p>

        <h3 class="career-step__subtitle">Five driving standards</h3>
        <p class="career-step__text">Once you&apos;re driving, you&apos;re held to these on every job:</p>
        <ol class="career-outcomes">
          <li><strong>Zero at-fault accidents.</strong> Always.</li>
          <li><strong>Maintain a passing Samara safe-driving score.</strong> Consistently.</li>
          <li><strong>Know your vehicle.</strong> Operate equipment and perform basic maintenance checks.</li>
          <li><strong>DOT paperwork, every time.</strong> Pre- and post-trip inspections and required logs — without exception.</li>
          <li><strong>Everyone feels safe.</strong> Your crew and the company trust you behind the wheel.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <figure class="career-step__media">
        <img src={IMG.cdlDriver} alt="Allied CDL driver in front of a truck" width="600" height="400" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="content-card career-path__pay" id="pay">
      <p class="section-label">Compensation</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">How pay progresses</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        When you complete Steps 1–4, you unlock a higher pay tier. From there, consistent
        performance moves you up again.
      </p>
      <div class="career-pay-tiers">
        <article class="career-pay-tier">
          <h3 class="career-pay-tier__name">Qualified</h3>
          <p class="career-pay-tier__desc">
            You&apos;ve met all requirements and are newly in the role — or you&apos;re experienced
            but still building consistency.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="career-pay-tier">
          <h3 class="career-pay-tier__name">Established</h3>
          <p class="career-pay-tier__desc">
            You&apos;ve hit all 10 key outcomes on at least 90% of your jobs for a minimum of
            <strong>6 continuous months</strong>.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="career-pay-tier">
          <h3 class="career-pay-tier__name">Experienced</h3>
          <p class="career-pay-tier__desc">
            You&apos;ve hit all 10 key outcomes on at least 90% of your jobs for a minimum of
            <strong>24 continuous months</strong>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="career-step__text career-path__pay-note">
        Each tier pays more than the last. Talk to your manager for current pay rates — they vary by
        location.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="career-payoff" id="future">
    <div class="career-payoff__inner">
      <div class="career-payoff__intro">
        <p class="career-payoff__label">What&apos;s next</p>
        <h2 class="career-payoff__title">Where this can take you</h2>
        <p class="career-payoff__lead">
          The path keeps climbing. Team leader is the foundation. CDL-A is a real career. Owner-operator
          is the top.
        </p>
      </div>

      <article class="career-altitude career-altitude--cdl">
        <p class="career-altitude__kicker">A real career</p>
        <h3 class="career-altitude__title">CDL-A driver</h3>
        <p class="career-altitude__text">
          Earn a CDL-A and run larger equipment. It&apos;s a legitimate career with significantly higher
          pay — and no business ownership required. Ask your manager for current CDL-A pay ranges at
          your location.
        </p>
        <a href={hrefPath("cdl-drivers/")} class="career-inline-link">
          Learn about hauling for Bailey&apos;s as a CDL driver →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="career-altitude career-altitude--summit">
        <p class="career-altitude__kicker">The summit</p>
        <h3 class="career-altitude__title">Owner-operator</h3>
        <p class="career-altitude__figure">
          <span class="career-altitude__number">$100,000–$200,000</span>
          <span class="career-altitude__figure-label">typical yearly earnings — and more is possible</span>
        </p>
        <p class="career-altitude__text career-altitude__text--summit">
          For a CDL-A driver, this is the single biggest income opportunity available. You own the
          truck. You run the business. What you earn follows what you put in.
        </p>

        <CareerPathStories />
      </article>

      <div class="career-path__cta">
        <h2 class="career-payoff__cta-title">Ready to take the next step?</h2>
        <p class="career-payoff__cta-lead">
          Frank, Troy, and the Himes already run this. Talk to your manager about where you stand —
          or apply and start the path that leads toward what they have.
        </p>
        <div class="home-cta-row">
          <a href={hrefPath("operations/")} class="btn btn-primary">See open operations roles</a>
          <a href={BRAND.phoneHref} class="btn btn-secondary">Call {BRAND.phone}</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CareersCrosslink />
</BaseLayout>
